    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean that's a bit vague. if you had to look at the actual data, wouldn't most economists agree that the net effect on the working class was negative because of how much manufacturing was lost to outsourcing? feels like the 'boost employment' argument is mostly just theory while the job losses actually happened.",
