      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some theories suggest broad employment gains, empirical studies on the direct impact of TPP on the domestic working class remain contested. Many analyses have highlighted the vulnerability of manufacturing jobs to increased international competition and outsourcing pressures, supporting your view of significant job displacement in certain sectors. However, other economic models point to growth in service sectors or higher-skill areas as offsetting effects, suggesting the net outcome was more nuanced than a simple loss.",
      "source": "target",
